1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,999
I'm about to record myself checking an invoice from our staffing vendor, so Ramp can learn how I review it.

2
00:00:07,502 --> 00:00:10,302
I'm checking this month's invoice from Halcyon Staffing.

3
00:00:11,986 --> 00:00:14,526
Every rate on it has to match our contract.

4
00:00:14,626 --> 00:00:17,239
And nobody should be billed twice for the same week.

5
00:00:17,339 --> 00:00:19,167
Then I check each person's hours against their timecard.

6
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:22,067
Maya is approved for 40 hours. Billed hours can't go over that.

7
00:00:25,742 --> 00:00:28,542
Sam is approved for 36.

8
00:00:28,898 --> 00:00:31,698
If anything is off, I dispute it and ask for a credit.

9
00:00:35,772 --> 00:00:41,172
While I work, the recorder saves each click with the exact element it hit.

10
00:00:41,372 --> 00:00:46,872
What I say is saved alongside, and passwords are blanked before they leave the page.

11
00:00:46,972 --> 00:00:50,372
When I'm done, I send the recording straight to Ramp.

12
00:00:50,572 --> 00:00:53,954
I sign in, and Ramp Teach starts learning from what I just did.

13
00:00:54,354 --> 00:01:02,918
A few seconds later it has the rules, written from my clicks and what I said.

14
00:01:03,118 --> 00:01:07,918
The agent sees each page as a short outline, with a tag on every element it can use.

15
00:01:08,118 --> 00:01:13,518
It picks an action, sees what changed, and goes again. Eight turns to read four timecards.

16
00:01:13,718 --> 00:01:18,218
It can't run scripts, upload files or leave the vendor's portal.

17
00:01:18,318 --> 00:01:23,297
Now a new invoice from the same vendor lands in Bill Pay.

18
00:01:23,697 --> 00:01:25,675
The agent picks it up on its own.

19
00:01:26,075 --> 00:01:37,475
It opens the vendor portal and checks each timecard, the same way I did.

20
00:01:37,675 --> 00:01:49,475
Every step it takes shows up on the bill as it happens.

21
00:01:49,675 --> 00:02:00,702
It checks billed hours, rates and duplicate lines against the contract.

22
00:02:01,002 --> 00:02:08,024
Then it writes up what it found.

23
00:02:08,324 --> 00:02:13,724
Three problems: a rate above contract, a line billed twice, and hours over the timecard. $3,448 to credit back.

24
00:02:13,924 --> 00:02:17,501
So I dispute it. The agent never approves or pays anything on its own.

25
00:02:17,601 --> 00:02:23,201
Plain code does the math. The agent's timecard facts settle the one check code can't do alone.

26
00:02:23,401 --> 00:02:30,001
Claude writes the receipt with a source for each problem, and only I can approve or dispute.

27
00:02:30,201 --> 00:02:37,420
Next, a clean invoice from the same vendor.

28
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:44,346
Same review, sped up.

29
00:02:44,466 --> 00:02:47,266
Everything checks out, so it's ready to approve.

30
00:02:47,466 --> 00:02:55,206
One click from me, and it moves on to payment.

31
00:02:55,306 --> 00:03:01,306
Every step writes a line to a log: what ran, and whether Claude, plain code or a person did it.

32
00:03:01,506 --> 00:03:08,706
Each Claude call is logged with its request ID, so it can be checked against Anthropic's own records.
